WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:05.680
You already know he sports a superior mustache
and is blessed with a nose for news, but there

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.700
are a few things you might not know about
San Diego's most beloved newsperson.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.360
This is the untold truth of Ron Burgundy.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:17.180
Of course, there could be no Ron Burgundy
without Will Ferrell, the actor and comedian

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:22.480
who enjoyed a triumphant seven-year run on
Saturday Night Live from 1995 to 2002.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:23.400
"Hey!

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:24.280
Hey!"

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:25.900
"What is it, Mr. Tarkanian?"

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.860
"Oh thank you, that's exactly the response
I'm lookin' for."

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.860
Ferrell has left his indelible mark on a number
of films and television shows including memorable

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:39.140
turns in Zoolander, Stranger than Fiction,
and The Office, to name just a few.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:44.059
He's a master at creating huge, bombastic
characters and he'll do just about anything

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:44.700
for a laugh.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:49.280
"But the last time I checked, we don't have
a whole lot of songs that feature the cowbell."

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:52.060
"I gotta have more cowbell, babe."

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:57.420
He can also infuse roles with heart and emotional
heft, as he demonstrated in the 2003 comedy

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:57.920
Elf.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:03.160
A man of many talents, Ferrell also created
the comedy website Funny or Die with frequent

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.220
collaborator Adam McKay.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:08.520
"Don't make fun of me crying."

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:11.480
"You'll be evicted."

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:18.390
What's more, he's served as an executive producer
on shows like Eastbound &amp; Down and Succession.

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:20.860
Much like Ron Burgundy, Ferrell really gets
around.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:26.320
Released in 2004, Anchorman: The Legend of
Ron Burgundy is one of the most eminently

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:28.100
quotable movies of all time.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:33.280
The now-classic film tells the story of you
guessed it Ron Burgundy, a local newscaster

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:34.100
in San Diego.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:38.750
His world is suddenly turned upside down by
the addition of newscaster Veronica Corningstone,

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:40.440
played by Christina Applegate.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:45.000
Ron is instantly smitten, and he has a really
interesting way of showing it.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:46.920
"You stay classy, San Diego."

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:48.840
"And thanks for stopping by."

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:51.260
"But mainly, stay classy."

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:52.840
"Thanks for stopping by."

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:54.360
"Stay classy, I"m Ron Burgundy."

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:59.439
Ferrell's performance makes the film work
seamlessly and the end result is a truly uproarious

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:00.780
and original comedy.

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:05.240
In fact, the bloody anchorman fight might
be one of the oddest sequences ever committed

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:06.120
to celluloid.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.200
"I stabbed a man in the heart."

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:09.960
"I saw that."

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:15.080
If you thought the original Anchorman was
crazy, it's got nothing on the sequel.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:20.420
Released in 2013, the film finds Ron and Veronica
working at a huge network in New York City.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:25.060
Harrison Ford plays newscaster Mack Tannen,
who announces his retirement and reveals he

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:27.740
wants to give his job to Veronica rather than
Ron.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:30.840
This development immediately drives a rift
between the couple.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.980
Burgundy temporarily leaves his wife and child
to join the first 24-hour news network alongside

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:40.660
his original team, facing off against younger,
more popular anchorman Jack Lime, portrayed

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:41.700
by James Marsden.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:46.060
There's even a second anchorman fight, which
is bigger and better than the first one.

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:50.870
We'd also be remiss not to mention the insane
subplot that finds Ron adopting a shark named

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:51.360
Doby.

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:56.000
While it never quite reaches the comedic heights
of the original, it's still a worthwhile film

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.480
— especially since it fully embraces its
own ridiculousness.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:00.560
"Check this out.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:03.340
This… this was fun.

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:05.460
We shot this over two weeks in Prague."

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:06.120
"Wow."

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:11.200
Ron Burgundy is based on a real person, and
his name is Mort Crim.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.650
The Philadelphia-born newsman spent decades
delivering the news.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:19.860
In 2009, Crim was even inducted into the Broadcast
Pioneers of Philadelphia's "Hall of Fame."

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.280
But what makes him so ripe for satire?

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:28.520
"Well you have to understand that I was a
typical traditional 1972 male chauvinist anchor."

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:33.840
In 2013, Ferrell admitted he was inspired
by Crim's voice and general look, and Crim

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:37.040
seems to have enjoyed the imitation, telling
USA Today:

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:41.380
"Any good parody takes a grain of truth and
exaggerates it for the big screen.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:44.840
People ask me if I'm offended at all and I
say not in the least."

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:48.520
As he told the Australian morning show Wake
Up in 2013,

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:55.400
"You know, I think Anchorman 1 was a very
good parody of how it was back in the seventies."

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.500
But no love for Anchorman 2: The Legend Continues?

00:03:58.700 --> 00:03:59.480
Interesting.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:02.860
You just never know when a little bit of Ron
will enter your life.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:08.320
During the promotional period for Anchorman
2 in 2012, Burgundy made a few memorable appearances

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:08.980
on Conan.

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:12.730
"Night in and night out, you guys get it done."

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:13.360
"Thank you."

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:18.900
He's also no stranger to the world of sports,
contributing his special brand of madness

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:23.520
to both the 2014 Sochi Olympics and a Los
Angeles Kings game in 2019.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:26.560
"They even brought me this ice-cold cup of
milk."

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:31.880
A true media maven, Ron Burgundy has also
appeared in a series of commercials for Dodge.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:34.220
"Get outta here, you dumb dancers!

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:37.600
I've told them a hundred times they can't
dance in here.

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:39.820
Buncha dirty dancers."

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:45.900
Last but not least, he appeared at the Comedy
Central's Roast of Justin Bieber in 2015.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:47.680
"Some real clever writing.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:48.580
Great energy over there."

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:52.220
Whatever the occasion, it's always a pleasure
to see Ron again.

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:58.040
In the summer of 2019, Will Ferrell really
ramped up his Ron Burgundy appearances, staging

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:00.160
an unexpected late-night takeover.

00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:05.080
On one random Thursday, six different shows
listed a "Surprise Guest" in their credits,

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:08.479
and that guest turned out to be none other
than Ron Burgundy.

00:05:08.479 --> 00:05:12.639
On Thursday, August 8th, Burgundy appeared
on The Late Show with Stephen Colbert, The

00:05:12.639 --> 00:05:17.150
Late Late Show with James Corden, The Tonight
Show Starring Jimmy Fallon, Conan, Late Night

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.280
with Seth Meyers, and Jimmy Kimmel Live!.

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:24.200
Burgundy was ostensibly making the rounds
to hone his so-called "comedy routine," which

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:26.940
— as you've probably guessed — is terrible.

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.660
"Have we got any Shawn Mendes fans here tonight?

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:34.100
Yeah, don't like him, never have."

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:36.880
"Oh I see, it's an anacronym."

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:44.320
All these appearances helped promote the second
season of The Ron Burgundy Podcast, and you

00:05:44.321 --> 00:05:46.090
can bet we've been tuning in.

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:49.009
We just can't get enough of his incisive worldview.

00:05:49.009 --> 00:05:51.900
"Why are tiny refrigerators called 'minibars'
in hotels?

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.460
I don't call bars 'giant refrigerators.'"

